### Re-measured independently on `origin/main` @ `abc4b83ce8b01d4e5af3560a0547421f6f5ca98f`, 2026-09-11T00:5xZ

The contract text, `packages/spec/src/data/search-fields.ts:8-9` — ⚠️ note this is the **post-PR #17572** wording (merged 2026-09-11T00:34:36Z), so the card's 「sharper than it was this morning」 is live on main right now:

> ` * - the ENGINE (@objectstack/objectql expandSearchToFilter), which expands`
> ` *   a $search term into a $or of $icontains clauses over exactly this set`

The engine, `packages/objectql/src/search-filter.ts:144-148`:

```ts
const hasCompanion = !!opts.fields[SEARCH_COMPANION_FIELD];
const andClauses = terms.map((term) => {
  const clauses = searchFields.flatMap((f) => fieldClausesForTerm(f, term, opts.fields[f] || {}));
  if (hasCompanion && isCompanionMatchableTerm(term)) {
    clauses.push({ [SEARCH_COMPANION_FIELD]: { $contains: term.toLowerCase() } });
  }
  return { $or: clauses };
});
```

⇒ ✅ both halves of the card hold: the `$or` carries a clause on a field **not in the set** (so 「exactly this set」 is false), and that clause is **`$contains`, not `$icontains`** (so the just-corrected bullet now over-generalises in the other direction).

### Why class (b) and not class (a)

A published `packages/spec` docblock describing engine behaviour the engine does not have. ⛔ Nothing fails when copied — no example, no reproduction — so it is not (a); the cited contract text is the docblock itself and the engine contradicts it, which is (b). Identical reasoning to #15052, ⛔ not a new reading.

### ⚠️ Fence for the taker — the deliberate `$contains` is the trap

`search-filter.ts:138-143` carries an explicit instruction at the site:

> *"This is a different mechanism from the source-column clauses in `fieldClausesForTerm`, which compare against raw stored text and therefore need `$icontains`. **Do not "align" the two.**"*

⇒ ⛔ **The fix is to the sentence, not to the engine.** A round that "aligns" the companion clause to `$icontains` would break a case-folded-on-both-sides comparison that is exact by construction. The deliverable is a docblock that says: `$icontains` over this set, **plus** — when the object carries the deployment-gated `__search` companion — one additional `$contains` clause on that companion, which is correct because both sides are already lowercase.

`Size/model suggestion:` S — one docblock, in the file the card names. ⚠️ ⛔ Do not widen to the engine.

